  nonce: '0049'  # 0049
  message: "DONE in PR #2389 (dev b26c7dcf7) and its follow-up PR #2393 (dev 66038a57a). Scope as built: calls AND instantiates (the description says calls only; a constructor call asks the same question, and call_construct already declares both types).\n\nAGAINST THE SIX CONDITIONS\n1. Vocabulary: hypergumbo_core/resolved_by.py, eleven values each with its statement; Edge.create(resolved_by=) raises on an undeclared value, on another edge type and on is_resolved=False (tests/test_resolved_by.py). Registered in axis_meta_keys (single writer, per call site).\n2. Every creation site: scripts/check-resolved-by-sites, gate test_resolved_by_sites.py::test_live_tree_is_clean. Re-run at 66038a57a: \"every call-family creation site is marked; old-spelling pins hold\". Not judged by it: 17 sites whose edge_type is not a literal (the two that can be call-family, SCIP and F#, were stamped by hand), and a site that passes is_resolved=False with its destination in a variable.\n3. Mark if and only if resolved: \"only if\" holds by construction (finalize removes the mark from an edge that leaves the repository). \"If\" is MEASURED, not constructed: 51 repositories, 271,323 resolved call-family edges, 0 with no mark, 400,522 unresolved, 0 with a mark (census_full_final.md). It is not asserted for producers those repositories do not reach; WI-pitok is the residual (no run-time gate; 26 linker sites with no value-pinning test).\n4. symbol_resolution: MATCH_* constants, LookupResult.resolved_by maps them in one place.\n5. Census: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/resolution_mark_11252026/census.py (in the lab notebook, not in the repository). By (type, language, mark) and by the number of declaring scopes holding a same-named symbol. Full set: calls 250,319 (name 72,678; receiver_type 71,244; own_type 24,873; same_file 20,733; qualified 14,995; import 13,604; same_module 12,241; lexical_scope 10,488; key_match 6,737; class_hint 2,036; after #2393 the 565 lua-ffi edges are name); instantiates 21,004 (name 17,636).\n6. No edge changed except the new key: 28 repositories, maps before the branch against maps at 1974add49, 28 of 28 identical with the key removed. The commits after that head were each checked on what they touch (COBOL fixture; libzmq; zstd, workadventure front and envoy api for #2393), not by a second 28-tree pass.\n\nWHAT THE MEASURING FOUND THAT THE STATIC CHECK COULD NOT (all fixed, all with tests that fail on the old code)\n- GraphQL (2 sites) and HTTP linkers passed the mark and then replaced edge.meta: found by widening check-meta-write-discipline rule 3, no such edge in the 28 trees.\n- Lua FFI phase 2 and two gRPC sites passed is_resolved=False for an in-repository target: 565 unmarked resolved edges on zstd, found only by the 51-tree census. The census run was 50 maps at b26c7dcf7 plus zstd again at 66038a57a (0 unmarked; edges and nodes identical to its b26c7dcf7 map with the key removed).\n- JavaScript, PHP, Lua, Zig and C# marked a call on an explicit receiver own_type; now name / qualified.\n\nNOT IN THIS ITEM, filed: readers (WI-topit), folds (WI-gilip), the guess-prone routes read during the stamping (WI-kanak, WI-mapas, WI-zibis, WI-hubaf, WI-fatad, WI-suhol, WI-bujih, WI-giroz, WI-patin)."  # 0049
